<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="StraightStraightNoChaser-F-Theme" spTempo="190">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1951
Composer:	Thelonious Monk
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Bebop blues
Key:	Eb major

“Straight, No Chaser” was composed and first recorded by
Thelonious Monk in 1951, becoming one of his best-known blues
compositions and a frequent jam-session vehicle. Its distinctive
melody uses rhythmic displacement and repeated blues figures;
later performances, including Miles Davis’s, are often transposed
to other keys.</spComments>
